CLOSURE_CHECKS_CLASSIFIER_AUDIT: {
  "schema_version": 1,
  "migration_run_id": "8b32109d-1521-469b-80aa-b273da3e8ddb",
  "snapshot_timestamp": "2026-05-22T00:54:20Z",
  "ticket_id": "bc7f-1a0d",
  "items": [
    {
      "original_text": "SC1. Running /dso:remediate --docs on a nava-platform project with a markdown file that contains a section reachable by zero inbound cross-references surfaces that section as a P-D1 candidate through the blue-team routing path.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system capability where the remediate tool identifies unreferenced sections through a specific routing path, phrased as ongoing behavior"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "SC2. Running /dso:remediate --tests on a nava-platform project with a test function whose assertions target only mock-interaction verification (no assertion with a non-mock left-hand side) surfaces that test as a P-T2 candidate through the blue-team routing path, across Python (python-ast), JS/TS (ast-grep), and Ruby (ast-grep) test files.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system capability where the remediate tool identifies and surfaces P-T2 candidates through specified routing paths across multiple languages"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "SC3. Running /dso:remediate --code on a nava-platform project with a function whose parameter is passed the same literal value at every call site surfaces that parameter as a P-C2 candidate through the blue-team routing path.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system capability (the remediate tool's ability to surface P-C2 candidates) phrased as ongoing behavior, though the technical jargon creates minor ambiguity"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "SC4. When the user selects Path B after a /dso:remediate run that surfaces P-D1, P-T2, or P-C2 candidates with CONFIRM verdicts, the resolver applies the appropriate action \u2014 delete_block/delete_file for P-D1, delete_function for P-T2, refactor_remove_param for P-C2 \u2014 with the new refactor_remove_param action implemented for Python, JS/TS, and Ruby.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system capability where the resolver applies specific actions for different candidate types, with new refactor_remove_param action supported across languages"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "SC5. Per-template fixtures at tests/fixtures/remediate/<template>/ (flask, nextjs, rails, jekyll-uswds) include expected candidates and expected-false-positive-safe items for each new pattern applicable to the template; automated validation asserts that the blue-team DISMISS rate across fixture candidates is <= 50% per pattern.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system property (fixture structure and automated validation behavior) that persists after completion, phrased as ongoing validation capability"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "SC6. The existing session-end summary at \\$ARTIFACTS_DIR/remediate-summary-<timestamp>.json reflects counts from the new patterns in its existing fields (auto_remediated, blue_team_dismissed, blue_team_needs_human, flagged_for_review, user_resolved, resolver_applied, resolver_no_change) without schema changes.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable property of the summary file format where existing fields reflect new pattern counts, establishing an ongoing system behavior rather than a one-time completion task"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "SC7. During the sprint, a dogfooding run executes /dso:remediate --docs, --tests, and --code against at least one nava-platform template and captures an attached before/after artifact reporting: (a) candidates surfaced per pattern, (b) blue-team CONFIRM/DISMISS/NEEDS_HUMAN counts per pattern, (c) Path B applications completed for P-C2 CONFIRMs, and (d) the list of noise artifacts actually removed. The artifact is attached to the epic at closure and confirms the capability reduced developer-observable noise in at least one real nava-platform template \u2014 not just fixture candidates.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "transitional",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a one-time validation activity to be executed during the sprint with artifact capture, not an ongoing system property"
      },
      "user_decision": "accept",
      "post_migration_section": "CC"
    }
  ]
}
